# Line endings are LF in the working tree on every platform, not only in the
# index.
#
# Git's `core.autocrlf=true` — the Windows default — stores LF and checks out
# CRLF. `scripts/generate-params.mjs` writes LF, so on a Windows clone all
# fourteen generated parameter files differed from their own generator by
# nothing but their line endings, `npm run params:check` called every one of
# them stale, and `npm run build` refused to run. A guarantee that a generated
# file matches its manifest cannot depend on which operating system checked it
# out.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so never converted either way.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.svg text eol=lf
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.ogg binary
*.webm binary
*.pdf binary
*.wasm binary
*.zip binary
